{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"RED reproduced locally with the real audited binary, and the \"go install produced no binary\"\nhypothesis is FALSIFIED by a discriminating three-way test.\n\nInstalled the exact pinned commit into a temp GOBIN with a temp Go toolchain:\n  go install github.com/hashicorp/terraform-config-inspect@2fb54c236733ee65ee877105d595c124c993c64d\n\nA) canary with NO binary on PATH:\n   Failed: REBAR_TERRAFORM_CONFIG_INSPECT_CANARY=1 but terraform-config-inspect is not on PATH\n   -> a DIFFERENT failure signature from CI's.\n\nB) canary WITH the real binary present and working:\n   AssertionError: assert 'abstain' == 'match'\n   -> EXACTLY the CI signature (job 101295228786, change 2674; and job 101290520693 on the\n      dependabot PR-merged tree).\n\nC) what a missing binary actually does to the corroborator:\n   outcome=abstain reason=no_tool reason_detail=executable_not_resolvable\n   `_resolve_executable` raises BEFORE any subprocess is spawned, so a missing binary can never\n   produce empty stdout and can never raise a JSONDecodeError.\n\nSo the CI failure happens WITH a working binary, not without one, and `go install` is not\nimplicated: its CI step logs ten successful module downloads and no error, and the test's\n`has_binary` guard passed (execution reached the assertion at line 429).\n\nACTUAL REASON, from a direct call against the real binary:\n   outcome=abstain  reason=version_skew  reason_detail=config_inspect_schema_skew\n\nThe producer contract cannot validate the tool it pins. Validating one real\n`terraform-config-inspect --json .` document against terraform_config_inspect.schema.json\nyields 15 violations in three classes:\n  /: 'required_core' | 'provider_configs' | 'diagnostics' is a required property   (omitempty)\n  /*/pos: 'column' is a required property; 'byte' is a required property           (SourcePos\n          at the pinned commit is exactly {Filename string, Line int})\n  /*/provider: {'name': 'aws'} is not of type 'string', 'null'                     (it is an object)\n\nLATENT SECOND LINK: upstream `dirFiles` builds fullPath = filepath.Join(dir, name), so\npos.filename echoes the directory argument. `_run` passes the ABSOLUTE snapshot path\n(terraform_corroborator.py:286), so filenames return absolute and _validate_positions rejects\nthem at terraform_corroborator.py:367 as path_outside_snapshot. Verified both ways against the\nreal tool: absolute dir arg -> \"filename\": \"/tmp/realtf/snap/main.tf\"; \".\" -> \"filename\":\n\"main.tf\". Fixing only the schema would move the abstain, not remove it.\n\nDE-RISKED BEFORE CODIFYING: with the corrected schema plus \".\" as the directory argument,\napplied in a throwaway harness against the real binary:\n  variable.region      -> match\n  variable.missing     -> abstain no_unique_address\n  module.vpc (source)  -> match\n  data.aws_ami.base    -> abstain no_unique_address   <- separate defect, filed as eaved-bronze-loris\nThe first two are exactly the canary's assertions. Dry-running the staged patch on file copies\ntakes the schema from 15 violations against the real binary to 0.\n\nThe test is NOT being softened: it keeps refusing to pass on abstain. The contract is being\ncorrected to describe the tool that is actually pinned."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788609286880360565,"uuid":"96d75cf0-b5b7-4505-97d9-b945e60d8a24"}